  "details": "- CVE-2026-86425: split a copy of the image list at the first NULL:\n  image in the PerlMagick Layers method to prevent a heap use-after-free\n- CVE-2026-86423: clone every image that appears more than once in a\n  PerlMagick image list, not only adjacent repeats, so the same image is\n  never linked into a list twice\n- CVE-2026-86424: open the delegate output file without following\n  symbolic links and check the write policy again after opening it, to\n  prevent a symlink race from bypassing the path policy\n- CVE-2026-34238: check the despeckle buffer size for integer overflow\n  to prevent a heap buffer overflow on 32-bit systems",
